          "body": "Heavy legs on easy runs usually get blamed on overtraining. Often it is something else.\n\nYour blood needs iron to carry oxygen to your muscles. When your iron stores drop, your legs stop getting the oxygen they need, so they feel dead and your heart rate climbs to make up for it. For runners, the legs are the first place low iron shows up.\n\nThe marker to check is ferritin, your stored iron. Many active women feel their best closer to 40 or 50, well above the bottom of the normal range.\n\nCAVA\u00c9 is iron that skips the gut. It dissolves on your tongue and goes straight to your bloodstream, so there is no pill sitting heavy before a run.\n\nSee the 5 reasons your ferritin stays stuck below.",
